%description:

TcpSpoof.isSYN:true-answer -- a listener answers the SYN of the spoof with a SYN-ACK.

The claim (TcpSpoof.ned): "Sends fabricated TCP packets. ... Compatible with both IPv4
(~Ipv4) and IPv6 (~Ipv6)." TcpSpoof::sendSpoofPacket() sends one segment at the time t: a
header of 20 bytes without options and data, with the window 16384, no ACK, and the SYN bit
of isSYN.

The claim (TcpSpoof.ned): "Whether to set the SYN bit on the packet".

The classes: true (the default: the segment is a SYN) and false (the segment has no
control bit at all). The code: TcpSpoof::sendSpoofPacket() sets the SYN bit from the value,
and no other bit. The facet true-answer: a SYN of the spoof is a segment that a TCP can take, so a listener
answers it. This test separates "true" from "false", where a listener sends no answer (RFC 9293
section 3.10.7.2). TcpSpoof::sendSpoofPacket() declares the checksum of its segments correct, the
default of Tcp, so Tcp::checkChecksum() of host2 accepts the segment.

Node under test: host1; host1 has TcpSpoof in place of its TCP and no application; host2
listens at the port 1000 (TcpEchoApp). The spoof sends one SYN at 1 s from the port 5000 to
host2:1000 with the sequence number 12345. Observation: level 1,
host2 answers with a SYN-ACK that acknowledges 12346.

%# parameter: TcpSpoof.isSYN
%# class: true-answer
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.isSYN
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpSpoofIsSYNTrueAnswer")
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.srcPort == 5000 && tcp.synBit == true")
             .describe("the SYN of the spoof")
             .within(1.1))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.ackNo == 12346")
             .describe("the SYN-ACK of host2")
             .within(0.1));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpSpoofIsSYNTrueAnswer compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.isSYN = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.typename = "TcpSpoof"
*.host1.numApps = 0
*.host1.tcp.srcAddress = ""
*.host1.tcp.destAddress = "host2"
*.host1.tcp.srcPort = 5000
*.host1.tcp.destPort = 1000
*.host1.tcp.seqNo = 12345
*.host1.tcp.isSYN = true
*.host1.tcp.t = 1s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpSpoofIsSYNTrueAnswer: PASS
